Puzzle | Matchstick

How to make 4 equilateral triangles with 6 identical matchsticks? 

Solution:

Method I: A tetrahedron has:

4 equilateral triangle faces
6 edges
4 vertices
Each edge of the tetrahedron can be formed with one matchstick.
So, arrange the 6 matchsticks to form a tetrahedron:
Take 3 matchsticks. Arrange them to form an equilateral triangle. This will be the base.
Take the remaining 3 matchsticks. Connect each vertex of the base triangle to a single common point above the base. This point is the apex.
Position the apex so that each of these three edges has the same length as the matchsticks forming the base.
The result is a tetrahedron, with 4 equilateral triangular faces and 6 equal edges.

Method II:

Use 3 matchsticks to make a large equilateral triangle (each matchstick forms one side).
Now take 3 more matchsticks and connect the midpoints of the triangle’s sides.
These 3 inner matchsticks form a smaller inverted triangle inside the larger one.

